# Google Sheets Sync Process

- Canonical sheet names and headers live in `api/config/domain/sheets.ts`; `api/config/domain.ts` is only the backward-compatible barrel. `api/config/domain/runtime.ts` applies `TEST_` prefixes to sheet env vars when `TEST_MODE=true`.
- Container IDs are env-driven: `MASTER_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `MASTER_BOOKED_SHEET_ID`, and source lead containers `TBM_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `TBM_PRIME_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `TOP10_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `BEST_RELOCATION_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `MAINSITE_LEADS_SHEET_ID`.

## Containers And Tabs

- Master Leads (`MASTER_LEADS_SHEET_ID`) has `Forms`, `Calls`, and `Duplicates`.
- Source lead sheets have `Forms`, `Calls`, and `Duplicates`; sources with `hasBadTabs=true` also have `Bad Leads` and `Bad Calls`. `main_site` has no bad tabs. `not_provided` has no source sheet target.
- Master Booked (`MASTER_BOOKED_SHEET_ID`) has `Booked Deals` and `Cancelled Deals`.

## Canonical Headers

- `Forms`, `Duplicates`, `Bad Leads`: `Timestamp`, `Name`, `Pickup Zip`, `Destination Zip`, `Pickup State`, `Delivery State`, `Move Date`, `Phone Number`, `Mongo ID`, `Ref No`, `Booked`, `Booked Date`, `OVER 2000`, `OVER 4000`, `Cancelled`, `Local`, `Cubic Feet`, `Source Company`, `Quoted`. (`Move Size`, `Lead ID`, and `Source Company Site` were removed; the Mongo fields still exist but are no longer projected.)
- `Calls`, `Bad Calls`: `Timestamp`, `Job No`, `Phone Number`, `Duration`, `Booked`, `Booked Date`, `Over 2000`, `Over 4000`, `Cancelled`, `Local`, `Cubic Feet`, `Mongo ID`, `Source Company`, `FormFill`.
- `Booked Deals`: `Timestamp`, `Agent`, `SplitAgent`, `Binder Amount`, `Split`, `Book Date`, `Job No`, `Customer Name`, `Deposit Amount`, `Merchant`, `Source`, `Mongo ID`, `Mongo Lead ID`, `Local`, `Cancelled`.
- `Cancelled Deals`: `Timestamp`, `Agent`, `Cancel Date`, `Job No`, `Customer Name`, `Refund Amount`, `Source`, `Mongo ID`, `Lead Mongo ID`.

## Write Targets

- Form/call lead writes are gated by `shouldWriteSourceLeadSheets()` (env `WRITE_SOURCE_LEAD_SHEETS`, default `false`). Default is **master-only**: source-company lead sheets are formula derivatives of the master. `getLeadTargets()` only appends the source target when the flag is enabled. Source-target plumbing (tabs, projections, delete fallback via `sheet_sync[]`) is retained either way.
- Form leads sync to master `Forms` (plus source `Forms` only when the flag is on); duplicate form leads sync to master `Duplicates` (plus source when enabled).
- Call leads sync to master `Calls` (plus source `Calls` only when the flag is on); call leads created only for unmatched bookings are skipped until real call data exists.
- Booked leads sync only to master `Booked Deals`, then their linked form/call lead is refreshed so mirrored booking fields stay aligned.
- Cancelled leads sync the booking chain first, then the cancellation row to master `Cancelled Deals`.

## Sync Mechanics

- MongoDB is the source of truth. Create/update Mongo documents first, then schedule `sheetSync` background work with `waitUntil`; delete sheet rows before deleting Mongo documents so `sheet_sync[]` metadata is still available.
- `api/services/sheetSync/` owns job scheduling, chain lookup, source-lead refresh, and persistence of `sheet_sync[]`. `api/services/googleSheets/` owns auth, target resolution, tab/header creation, row projection, upsert, delete, and diagnostics.
- Before each target write, ensure all required tabs exist and rewrite canonical headers. Use `Mongo ID` as row identity; `sheet_sync[].row_number` is only a cached hint and must be verified before update/delete, otherwise scan by `Mongo ID`.
- Store one `sheet_sync[]` entry per target with target, spreadsheet ID, tab name, row number, `synced`/`failed`, last sync time/error, and dirty state. Partial failures keep successful targets as `synced` and failed targets as `failed`.
- Do not add CPL columns to Sheets. Use projection helpers for owner-facing values such as `booked`, `quoted`, `cancelled`, `local`, and threshold markers.
